{{/*
  The public chrome. Every file under templates/pages/ is rendered inside this
  one: the handler executes "layout" from that page's own template set, and the
  page supplies "content".

  Two blocks are the whole extension mechanism. A block is a default definition and
  the place it renders, written together — so this file says what a page may fill
  in, and a page that fills in nothing still renders correctly. Because each page
  gets its own set, a definition in one page reaches this layout on that page and
  nowhere else.

    content    the page itself. Every page defines it.
    nav_extra  an addition to the site nav, for a page that has one. Empty by
               default, which is what most pages want.

  The cost of the block form is that a page which defines neither renders an empty
  shell rather than failing, so ParseTemplates asserts at startup that every page
  defines "content". A page that forgets is a boot failure, not a blank page.
*/}}
{{define "layout"}}
{{template "document_head" .}}
<body>
<header class="site-header">
  <div class="inner">
    {{/*
      The mark is a bundled asset. Drop your own logo.svg into STATIC_DIR to replace
      it — the URL carries a hash of the file, so the new one appears immediately
      rather than after a cache expires.
    */}}
    <a class="brand" href="/">
      <img src="{{asset "logo.svg"}}" alt="" width="28" height="28">
      {{.SiteName}}
    </a>
    <nav>
      <a href="/events">Events</a>
      {{block "nav_extra" .}}{{end}}
      {{/*
        The account menu, for a browser signed in to the admin: fetched rather than
        rendered, so this page is the same for everybody and stays cacheable, and
        the admin session — whose cookie is scoped to /admin — is never needed
        here. A visitor with no session gets an empty 204 and sees nothing.
      */}}
      <span class="account-slot" hx-get="/admin/account/menu" hx-trigger="load"
            hx-swap="outerHTML"></span>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
<main>
<div class="inner">
{{block "content" .}}{{end}}
</div>
</main>
<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="inner columns">
    <div>
      <strong>{{.SiteName}}</strong>
      <p class="muted"><small>Powered by goevent.</small></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
{{end}}
